Security: Confine locally sourced app packages to the catalog directory

The address of an app package comes from the catalog response, i.e. from the
other end. HttpService::downloadApp() turned that into a local path without
confining it:

- `file://...` was accepted in every mode, including against the remote
  marketplace. A catalog entry reading
  `file:///var/www/owncloud/config/config.php` therefore fed an arbitrary local
  file into the app installer instead of delivering a package.
- In local-catalog mode a relative path was appended to the catalog directory
  unchecked - `../../..` walked straight out of it - and an absolute path was
  taken verbatim.

A local path is now accepted only in local-catalog mode, and only if it resolves
to a file inside the catalog directory; anything else is refused. Outside that
mode only `http://` and `https://` are allowed, matched on the full scheme
rather than the `http` prefix, which also matches `httpfoo://`.

The bundled catalog points at an https address, so nothing in the field depends
on a path outside the catalog directory.

This is the copy of the app bundled in apps-external/. The same change went to
BWTECH-github/market, where it carries the unit tests (72 tests; counter-checked
by disabling the containment, which turns three of them red).
